#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
bd-spawn-local-seat — Boylenet O1740 Headless Local GPU Seat Spawner & Dispatcher Adapter.

Spawns a headless BD_MAX_TURNS=20 (Rule 77) local fleet worker/reviewer/investigator seat
(--role builder|fixer|review-security|review-correctness|investigator,
 --tier tier1|tier2|tier3|auto, --task <path_or_prompt>, --seat-id <id>)
backed by the 4-Node Tesla T4 (64 GB GDDR6 VRAM) + 1.73 TB Locked DDR4 RAM Local GPU Cluster
(:4010 / :4000) with:
  1. Dynamic O1740 pool resolution from /home/mboyle/bd-persist/POOL_STATE.tsv (Rule 6: UNKNOWN != permission)
  2. Automatic registration & event publication on bd-bus WAL (/var/tmp/bd-bus.db & /home/mboyle/bd-persist/fleet-bus.db)
  3. Automatic Rule 74 (<=50 tokens: <STATUS> <path>) or Rule 76 ({"round":...,"seat":...,"verdict":"BOARD|REFUTE","findings":[]}) output contract enforcement
  4. Automatic Turn-20 RESUME_STATE.md checkpointing (Rule 77)
  5. Full compatibility with bd-say.sh (live tmux session with prompt & inbox consumer) and seat status inspection
"""
